# Conflict Resolution Workflow

## Purpose
Provide facilitators with clear recovery guidance when synchronization conflicts occur.  
This workflow was added after evaluation feedback showed that "Conflict Detected" alone was too vague.

## Steps

1. Retry Sync
   - Attempt synchronization again to resolve temporary connection issues.
   - System displays progress and confirms success or failure.

2. Check Offline Records
   - Review locally stored data to ensure attendance counts are correct.
   - Confirm that no personal identifiers are present (FR-08 compliance).

3. Escalate to Team Support
   - If conflict persists, notify the team representative.
   - Provide conflict details (timestamp, record ID, state) for resolution.

## Traceability
- Requirement: FR-08 (Privacy – numeric-only attendance)
- Prototype Element: Conflict Detected state in SyncQueue
- Evaluation Finding: Testers requested clearer recovery guidance
- Improvement: Structured conflict resolution workflow documented here
